    "case_id": "485",
    "case_summary": "A 55-year-old man with severe dilated cardiomyopathy and a left ventricular assist device (LVAD; HeartMate II) implanted four years previously was admitted for evaluation of low-grade fever. His serum creatinine had increased from 124 μmol/L to 354 μmol/L over two months, and he developed urinary protein excretion of 2.2 g/day with microhaematuria.\n\nPhysical examination was unremarkable.\n\n{'Laboratory Tests': ['- Serum creatinine: 354 μmol/L (increased from baseline of 124 μmol/L)', '- Elevated C-reactive protein and procalcitonin', '- Urinary protein excretion: 2.2 g/day', '- Microhaematuria without dysmorphic erythrocytes or casts', '- Blood cultures: positive for Corynebacterium jeikeium', '- Low serum complement C3 concentrations', '- Elevated PR3-ANCA and rheumatoid factor concentrations', '- Negative anti-MPO-ANCA'], 'Imaging Studies': {'18F-FDG PET-CT': 'Multiple foci of increased metabolic activity at the LVAD driveline insertion site, the ventricular assist device pocket, and the LVAD outflow cannula'}, 'Pathology': {'Renal Biopsy': {'Light Microscopy': \"23 glomeruli examined: 6 globally sclerotic, 10 segmentally sclerotic, cellular, and filling Bowman's space circumferentially. Non-sclerotic glomerular segments showed increased mesangial matrix and mesangial cells. 80% of the cortex and outer medulla had chronic tubulointerstitial damage.\", 'Immunohistology': 'Positive mesangial staining for IgM, C1q, and C3. Negative for IgA and IgG. Some glomerular basement membranes stained for C3 without humps.', 'Electron Microscopy': 'Mesangial regions with increased matrix and segmental subendothelial and mesangial osmiophilic deposits', 'Images': {'Figure 1A': 'Light microscopy showing necrosis with neighboring fibrocellular crescent', 'Figure 1B': 'Electron microscopy showing focal segmental necrotising immune-complex glomerulonephritis with subendothelial deposits'}}}}",
